{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"ecacc6cb07e3219b","name":"card_event_engage_range","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/NavalWarfare/events/card_event_engage_range","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"ENGAGE AT RANGE","text":"Deal 2 damage to an enemy. Convert into ENGAGE UP CLOSE if put from your hand to deck.","flavorText":"The Type 93 torpedo, nicknamed the “Long Lance”, was a powerful and advanced Japanese naval torpedo used during WWII. It was introduced in the 1930s and was fueled by compressed oxygen, giving it a much longer range, higher speed, and bigger warhead than Allied torpedoes of the time. With a range of up to 40 km (25 miles) and a warhead weighing around 490 kg (over 1,000 lbs), the Type 93 was extremely deadly. It could travel at high speeds with minimal wake, making it hard to detect. It was mostly launched from Japanese cruisers and destroyers, giving them a significant edge in night battles. The torpedo was especially effective early in the war, contributing to Japanese victories at Savo Island, Guadalcanal, and other Pacific battles. However, its long-range capabilities were not always fully used due to poor Japanese communication and targeting systems. Despite these flaws, the Type 93 was the most advanced torpedo of its time and a major threat to Allied naval forces throughout the war.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_engage_range","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_engage_range_title","SourceString":"ENGAGE AT RANGE","LocalizedString":"ENGAGE AT RANGE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_engage_range_text","SourceString":"Deal 2 damage to an enemy. Convert into ENGAGE UP CLOSE if put from your hand to deck.","LocalizedString":"Deal 2 damage to an enemy. Convert into ENGAGE UP CLOSE if